Decide
/ Decide which module and which action every step of this goal uses — the whole goal in two
/ exchanges, not one LLM call per step.
/
/ The decider is generic: it takes a state and typed questions and answers them. It knows nothing
/ about goals or steps. Everything goal-shaped is composed HERE.
/
/ The state is built as a plang value, not rendered as JSON text: it carries step text and module
/ prose, and prose contains quotes. A value serializes itself; text pasted into a JSON template
/ does not. The questions are rendered, because they only hold module names, action names and step
/ numbers, and they point at the state by path rather than repeating it.
/
/ Stage 1 asks a yes/no of every (step, module) pair at once. Independent answers mean a step that
/ uses three modules gets three yeses, instead of the model ranking them against each other and
/ dropping two. Stage 2 then asks a closed choice — which action — only of the modules that said
/ yes, and only where the module has more than one action to choose between.

- set %threshold% = 0.5
- set %modules% = %!app.module.list%

- set %state.goal% = %goal.Name%
- foreach %goal.Step%, call AddStepToState step=%item%
- foreach %modules%, call AddModuleToState module=%item%

- render template "/system/builder/llm/templates/deciderModuleQuestions.template", write to %moduleQuestions%
- llm.decider State=%state%, Question=%moduleQuestions%, write to %moduleAnswer%

- render template "/system/builder/llm/templates/deciderActionQuestions.template", write to %actionQuestions%
- llm.decider State=%state%, Question=%actionQuestions%, write to %actionAnswer%

- call /system/builder/EmitBuildEvent kind="goal-decided", goal=%goal%


AddStepToState
/ The decider sees a step as its position and its words — nothing it has been compiled into yet.
- add {"index": %step.Index%, "text": %step.Text%} to %state.step%


AddModuleToState
/ What each module is for, in its own words: the description the module ships with.
- set %state.modules% key %module.Name% to %module.Description%
